but it isn't because it's separate. They just say, hey, do this and then Congress does it. So it's not a cartel because they're two separate organizations that this is the system, guys. So it got the inefficiency of a centrally planned economy combined with the lack of accountability of a private capture model. And it has the absence of any redistribution towards unmet need that you would expect a centrally planned system to provide.

