00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:45.000
starts and stops there, you've made a horrible reduction of what psychology is. What I'm arguing is that the reason that CBT became the only thing that the apparatus could see at this point. Cognitive behavioral therapy was developed by Aaron Beck and Albert Ellis in the late 50s and 60s. And again, I'm not indicting these guys.

102
00:55:45.000 --> 00:56:06.000
What I'm saying is that the success of CBT, and they were very lucky, you know, it became the only thing the apparatus could see. And the apparatus started actively preventing the development of anything that wasn't it, you know, for the next 30 years, at least. Some people tell me that that's actually not true anymore, the last 15, whatever, whatever.

